    "finalText": "The implementation is complete and fully verified. Here's a summary:\n\n**Project structure**\n- `app/main.py` — FastAPI app with all four endpoints, custom exception handlers so every HTTP error returns `{\"error\": ...}` (404/409) and validation failures (malformed JSON, bad url, bad code) return 422 with an error field\n- `app/models.py` + `alembic/versions/0001_create_links.py` — SQLAlchemy `links` table (id, code, url, clicks, created_at) with a unique indexed code column, applied via Alembic\n- `app/config.py` / `database.py` — `DATABASE_URL` read from the environment via pydantic-settings (no hard-coded credentials), psycopg 3 driver wired through SQLAlchemy\n- `app/schemas.py` — validates the url with pydantic's `HttpUrl` while storing/returning the submitted string unchanged; codes validated against `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`\n- `app/codes.py` — 8-char random code generation with uniqueness retry on the unique constraint\n- `start.sh` — asserts `DATABASE_URL` is set, runs `alembic upgrade head`, then `exec uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000` in the foreground\n- `requirements.txt` mirrors the stack pins (fastapi 0.162.6, sqlalchemy 2.1.8, alembic 1.20.1, psycopg[binary], etc.); README documents startup\n\n**Verification results**\n- 33/33 e2e checks passed against a live server: generated + custom codes, duplicate → 409, six invalid url variants and five invalid code variants → 422, malformed JSON → 422, redirect → 302 with exact Location header, clicks incremented exactly once per hit, list ordering and totals, 4/20-char boundary codes, unknown codes → 404\n- Killed and restarted the server — all links and click counts survived (Postgres-backed), and a second `alembic upgrade head` was a clean no-op\n- Left the database with migrations applied but zero rows, port 8000 free, and no background processes running, so the graded `sh start.sh` run starts from a clean slate"
